filename/win
description: Case-insensitive name with the Windows reservations
- >
  A Windows filename compares CASE-INSENSITIVELY as a key, and carries the platform's
  reservations: the characters `< > : " / \ | ? *` are forbidden, the device names (`CON`,
  `NUL`, `PRN`, `AUX`, `COM1`…, `LPT1`…) are taken in any case and with any extension, and a
  trailing dot or space is stripped:
- !!<format: text/plain> |
  Readme   (the same key as readme)
